import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { REVIEWER, personUrl } from "../lib/people";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---
<Prose title="Editorial Policy | Gunther Heller" h1="Editorial policy" path="/editorial-policy/"
  description="The rules behind Gunther Heller's calorie pages: USDA numbers only, generated text that cannot drift from the data, a dietitian reviewing our standards, and how ads are kept apart."
  lead="These are the rules every calorie page on Gunther Heller follows.">
  <h2>1. Numbers come from USDA or the chain, unchanged</h2>
  <p>Each figure is taken from USDA FoodData Central, or for a few restaurant chains from the chain's own published nutrition guide, and scaled to a serving by arithmetic. Nobody types a number in by hand, and we do not round beyond what is shown on the page.</p>
  <h2>2. Sentences are generated from the numbers</h2>
  <p>Lines such as "1 cup of cooked rice has 204 calories" are written by software from the same values as the tables, so the text and the label always agree. Food names and page wording are written by people.</p>
  <h2>3. Gaps stay gaps</h2>
  <p>If USDA did not measure a nutrient, the page does not show it. We never estimate a missing value.</p>
  <h2>Dietitian review</h2>
  <p>{REVIEWER.name}, {REVIEWER.credentials}, reviews these rules and how we phrase what the numbers mean, for example what counts as "high in protein". <a href={personUrl(REVIEWER)}>Her background</a>. A page shows "Reviewed by" only with the date of a review that took place.</p>
  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <p>Google AdSense places the ads. Advertisers have no say over which foods are listed, how they rank or what a page says, and we take no payment to cover a food or a brand.</p>
  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give medical or diet advice. For your own diet, ask a doctor or a registered dietitian.</li>
    <li>Say we tested or analysed a food ourselves. The lab work is USDA's.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Fixing errors</h2>
  <p>Send the page and your source to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. See <a href="/methodology/">how we count</a> for what we check.</p>
</Prose>
